The companion mods above are compatible with Neon Fitting Room but may have their own requirements or compatibility notes. Check their pages before combining several of them.

[size=4][b]◈ INSTALLATION ◈[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install the required dependencies.
[*]Extract the entire Neon Fitting Room ZIP into the Cyberpunk 2077 game directory.
[*]Merge its [b]archive[/b] and [b]r6[/b] folders with the game's existing folders.
[*]Enter Photo Mode and open the V or NPC character page.
[/list]

The release build does not require or include a shared [i]Logs.reds[/i] file.

[size=4][b]◈ KNOWN BEHAVIOR ◈[/b][/size]

Neon Fitting Room is session-based. Leaving Photo Mode clears expanded panels, search text, scroll positions, manual clothing previews, and NPC selections. Re-entering Photo Mode starts from the outfits and character options supplied by the game and installed mods.

[color=#FF6B6B][b]NPC FIT LIMITATION[/b][/color]

Experimental NPC Clothing is disabled by default. When enabled through [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], supported NPCs receive a searchable, slot-based clothing browser, Clear, per-NPC session state, and an NPC component browser for toggling appearance-owned clothing, accessories, and hair.

The Clothing control appears only when the NPC's effective character record has compatible [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/6945]Equipment-EX[/url] attachment slots. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/6945]Equipment-EX[/url] provides them for a limited set of player-like NPCs. The optional [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/31327]NPC Outfit Manager[/url] adds them to more character records that already have a Chest slot. Neon Fitting Room reads the available slots; it does not add missing slots itself.

Compatible slots do not guarantee a compatible body. Most clothing is fitted for V and may clip through standard or modded NPC bodies. Neon Fitting Room does not dynamically refit meshes.

With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], you can change card density and enable or disable tooltips, outfit icons, and NPC Clothing. Without it, Neon Fitting Room uses eight cards per row, enables tooltips and outfit icons, and leaves NPC Clothing disabled.

Users with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] can enable NPC Clothing for the current game process without [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url]:

[code]Game.GetScriptableServiceContainer():GetService(CName.new("NeonFittingRoom.NfrConfig")):SetNpcClothingEnabled(true)[/code]

Run the command before entering Photo Mode, or leave and re-enter Photo Mode afterward. The override resets when the game restarts. Replace [i]true[/i] with [i]false[/i] to turn it off again.

